---
import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';

const jsonLd = {
  "@context": "https://schema.org",
  "@type": "WebPage",
  "name": "AdhocX Terms & Conditions of Commercial Service",
  "url": "https://www.adhocx.com/terms"
};
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Terms & Conditions of Service | AdhocX"
  description="Terms governing AdhocX corporate bookings, commercial driver partnership, dispatch cutoff SLAs and contractual refund obligations."
  canonical="https://www.adhocx.com/terms"
  activeNav="terms"
  breadcrumbs={[
    { name: 'Home', url: '/' },
    { name: 'Terms of Service', url: '/terms' }
  ]}
  jsonLd={jsonLd}
>
  <section class="legal-page-section">
    <div class="legal-page-container">
      <div class="legal-header">
        <h1 class="legal-title">Terms & Conditions</h1>
        <p class="legal-meta">Last Updated: October 2026 &bull; Effective Version 3.1</p>
      </div>

      <div class="legal-content-card">
        <h2 id="operating-model">1. Commercial Marketplace Operating Model</h2>
        <p>
          AdhocX operates an automated, programmatic B2B dispatch and fulfillment marketplace connecting corporate enterprises ("Enterprise Bookers") with licensed commercial vehicle operators and independent chauffeurs ("Driver Partners") across Telangana (Hyderabad Tech Corridors & Regional Hubs). AdhocX enforces commercial motor vehicle compliance, transparent fixed tariffs, and programmatic dispatch telemetry.
        </p>

        <h2 id="compliance">2. Yellow-Board Commercial Fleet Requirements & Telangana Compliance</h2>
        <p>
          AdhocX exclusively permits commercial yellow-plate motor cabs in 4-seater (Sedan) and 6/7-seater (MUV/SUV) categories in compliance with Section 66 of the Motor Vehicles Act, 1988 and Section 23 of the Telangana Shops and Establishments Act, 1988 (G.O.Ms.No. 40). Private white-board passenger vehicles are strictly prohibited from commercial fulfillment.
        </p>
        <ul>
          <li>Drivers must possess a valid Commercial Driving License with required state transport authority badges (including Telangana RTO commercial badges and regional transport badges).</li>
          <li>Vehicles must maintain up-to-date third-party and passenger commercial insurance, fitness certificates, and pollution control compliance.</li>
          <li>Driver Partners agree to adhere to corporate safety standards, passenger dignity policies, and speed limit adherence.</li>
        </ul>

        <h2 id="refunds">3. Dispatch Cutoff Windows & Refund Terms</h2>
        <p>
          When an Enterprise Booker initiates a ride or shift requirement on the AdhocX platform, our dispatch engine searches for verified fleet partners within configured dispatch windows (configurable per corporate policy between 5 and 120 minutes, with a 30-minute system default, or a targeted 15-minute window for spot bookings). If a ride cannot be confirmed within the applicable window, the booking transitions to unfulfilled, and held funds are immediately credited back to the corporate escrow ledger. For corporate clients holding bank refund terms in their enterprise contract, bank refund instructions are initiated via IMPS/NEFT rails within an agreed 1-hour verification SLA window.
        </p>

        <h2 id="milestones">4. Driver Partner Milestone Incentive Terms</h2>
        <p>
          Newly verified Driver Partners are eligible for the introductory Milestone promotional incentive program. Upon completing one hundred (100) verified, non-fraudulent trips within thirty (30) calendar days from account activation, the milestone incentive will be deposited directly into the driver's verified bank account in the subsequent payout cycle. AdhocX reserves the right to audit trips against GPS logs to prevent fraudulent trip completions.
        </p>

        <h2 id="jurisdiction">5. Governing Law & Dispute Resolution</h2>
        <p>
          This Agreement shall be governed by and construed in accordance with the laws of the Republic of India. Any disputes arising out of or in connection with this platform shall be subject to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts in Hyderabad, Telangana, India. For questions regarding these terms, please review our <a href="/privacy">Privacy Policy</a> or reach our team via <a href="/contact">Contact & Demo Request</a>.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
</BaseLayout>
